                "title": "fix(discussion): resolve org-wide discussion URLs",
                "body": "fix(discussion): resolve org-wide discussion URLs\n\ngithub.com canonicalizes org-wide discussions to\n`/orgs/<org>/discussions/<n>`, so `URL_ISSUE_PATTERN` parsed the repo as\n`orgs/<org>` and the GraphQL lookup failed. The URL now maps to\n`<org>/<org>`.\n\n```\n:Octo https://github.com/orgs/community/discussions/144793\n```\n\nThe real repo is the org's user-chosen source repository\n(https://docs.github.com/en/organizations/managing-organization-settings/enabling-or-disabling-github-discussions-for-an-organization),\nwhich is not always `<org>/<org>` (e.g. `Homebrew/discussions`).\n`<org>/<org>` is the common case and there is no API to look the source\nrepo up from the URL alone; the comment on `resolve_org_url_repo` spells\nout the caveat.\n\nAlso applies to link navigation from the cursor via\n`extract_issue_at_cursor`, and to GHE hostnames.\n",
